title: Immigration and Nationality
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/heathrow.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and immigration_timer <= 0
on-arrival: immigration_timer = 6; month_actions += 1

= Immigration and Nationality

[? if swamped_seen = 1 : Your remark about people being afraid of being "swamped" won us votes in 1978. Now the government has to decide what it means in practice. ?][? if swamped_seen = 0 : The manifesto promised firm immigration control. Now the government has to decide what that means in practice. ?] [? if riots >= 1 : Since the riots, the inner cities have been watching too. ?]

- @nationality: Introduce a British Nationality Bill.
- @tighten_rules: Tighten the immigration rules.
- @boat_people: Take in Vietnamese boat people.
- @refuse_boat_people: Refuse to take more boat people.
- @race_relations: Fund community projects in the inner cities.
- @firm_line: Promise firm and fair immigration control.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@nationality
view-if: nationality_act = 0 and bill_nationality = 0 and time >= bill_nationality_wait
subtitle: The right is pleased; the wets and the Liberals are not. Law in about seven months.
choose-if: bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ bill_room_text +]
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 5; wet_dissent += 4; lib_relation -= 2; bill_new = "nationality"
call: bill_introduce

[+ home_secretary +] publishes the British Nationality Bill. It will replace citizenship of the United Kingdom and Colonies with three new categories, and only British citizens will have the automatic right to live here. Hong Kong notices.

@tighten_rules
view-if: immigration_rules < 2
subtitle: The right approves; the Liberals and the wets object.
choose-if: immigration_rules = 0 or home_dry = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ home_secretary +] won't go any further.
on-arrival: immigration_rules += 1; right_dissent -= 3; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent += 2; lib_relation -= 2

[? if immigration_rules = 1 : Women settled here lose the automatic right to bring in husbands from abroad, under a new "primary purpose" rule. ?][? if immigration_rules = 2 : Entry clearance checks are tightened and appeals restricted. The queues at the High Commission in Dhaka grow longer. ?]

@boat_people
view-if: boat_people = 0 and time <= 30
subtitle: Our allies are grateful. The right is not.
on-arrival: boat_people = 1; us_relation += 4; europe_relation += 2; lib_relation += 2; wet_dissent -= 2; right_dissent += 3
achievement: boat_people

At the Geneva conference, Britain agrees to take ten thousand refugees from the camps in Hong Kong. Willie Whitelaw insists it is the decent thing to do, and you let him win the argument.

@refuse_boat_people
view-if: boat_people = 0 and time <= 30
subtitle: The right approves. The Americans and the wets do not.
on-arrival: boat_people = -1; right_dissent -= 2; us_relation -= 4; lib_relation -= 2; wet_dissent += 3

We tell the Geneva conference that Britain has already done enough by keeping the camps in Hong Kong open. The Americans and the Australians are unimpressed.

@race_relations
view-if: race_relations = 0
subtitle: -0.5 budget. The wets approve; the right calls it a waste.
on-arrival: race_relations = 1; budget -= 0.5; wet_dissent -= 3; right_dissent += 2; de_con += 1*(1-dissent); c1_lib -= 1

Money from the Urban Programme goes to community centres, youth projects and the Commission for Racial Equality. [? if riots >= 1 : It is the least that Lord Scarman will expect. ?]

@firm_line
subtitle: The right is reassured. The wets and the Liberals wince.
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent += 2; c2_con += 0.5*(1-dissent); lib_relation -= 1

[+ home_secretary +] tells the party conference that control is firm and that it will stay firm. The numbers settling here each year change little, and the speech is mostly for the hall.
